  "id": "Compound::DB00705 - Gene::1565",
  "verbalization": "Delavirdine is a non-nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor (NNRTI) that is included in the class of Organonitrogen Heterocyclic Compounds and Non-Nucleoside Reverse Transcriptase Inhibitors. This class includes Efavirenz, which binds to Cyp2d6, a cytochrome P450 enzyme involved in the metabolism of various substrates. The shared lowest common ancestor of Delavirdine and Efavirenz is the Organonitrogen Heterocyclic Compound category, reinforcing the classification as a non-nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor. The evidence suggests that Delavirdine may interact with Cyp2d6 through a mechanism involving its binding to the enzyme, potentially affecting its metabolic activity. The integration of these paths highlights a possible pathway where Delavirdine influences Cyp2d6, possibly through direct interaction or through a shared metabolic pathway. The mechanism is supported by the presence of Cyp2c19, which participates in arachidonic acid epoxygenase activity, and Cyp2d6, suggesting a broader metabolic network. The evidence is consistent with a mechanistic link between Delavirdine and Cyp2d6, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact nature of the interaction.",
